<title>GERMANY: EU rapeseed crush seen headed for three-year low.</title>
<headline>EU rapeseed crush seen headed for three-year low.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Processing of rapeseed in the European Union is forecast to fall to a three-year low of 6.45 million tonnes in July/June 1996/97, the independent Oil World newsletter said.</p>
<p>Crushings in 1995/96 totalled 8.02 million tonnes and 7.23 million in 94/95.</p>
<p>The publication said the final figure could be even lower given that the 1996 crop had been sharply down, especially in Germany and Scandinavia, and its oil content was also reduced.</p>
<p>EU rapeseed imports were declining while exports to Poland and other third countries were being maintained.</p>
<p>EU production of rape oil in July/December 1996 dropped by 23 percent on the same 1995 period to 1.31 million tonnes.</p>
<p>Oil World gave the following estimates for EU rapeseed --</p>
<p>    (in '000 tonnes)		   96/97	    95/96</p>
<p>    Carry-in stocks		     420		343</p>
<p>    Crop				  7,132	    8,233</p>
<p>    Imports, excl. intra-EU	   366		882</p>
<p>    Exports, excl. intra-EU	   500		125</p>
<p>    Crushings			   6,450	    8,018</p>
<p>    Other uses			    700		895</p>
<p>    Ending stocks			 268		420</p>
<p>-Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
